ngm:two-heads-are-better-than-one a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Two Heads Are Better Than One"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Two Heads Are Better Than One is the principle that collaborative or ensemble approaches to problem-solving outperform individual effort, applied in AI contexts to multi-agent systems, ensemble methods, and human-in-the-loop architectures. It underpins debate-based reasoning, peer-review agent patterns, and consensus mechanisms where diverse model outputs are aggregated to improve accuracy and reduce error."@en ;
