    rdfs:comment "GPU Acceleration is the use of graphics processing units to perform general-purpose computational workloads in parallel, exploiting the thousands of smaller cores present in a GPU to achieve throughput far exceeding that of conventional CPUs for data-parallel tasks. It is the dominant execution paradigm for training and inference in modern deep learning systems."@en ;
