ngm:ros-2 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "ROS 2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "ROS 2 (Robot Operating System 2) is an open-source robotics middleware framework developed by Open Robotics that provides a standardised publish-subscribe communication layer built on the DDS (Data Distribution Service) standard, along with a comprehensive ecosystem of drivers, libraries, and tools for sensor integration, motion planning, simulation, and hardware abstraction. ROS 2 supersedes ROS 1 with support for real-time execution, multi-robot systems, production-grade security via DDS-Security, and native Windows and macOS compatibility. It has become the de facto standard software framework for research and increasingly for commercial robotic platforms."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ngm:middleware,
